# Dashboards (P10.1 + P10.6) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development) is the same as users.http. Both dashboards are composed in the host from module
# contracts; a section/metric whose source fails comes back null and is listed in "unavailable".

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminToken = paste-the-admin-token-here
@studentToken = paste-a-students-token-here
@termId = paste-the-active-term-id-here
@facultyId = paste-a-faculty-id-here

### Student: home screen — today's lectures, next lecture, assignments due in 7 days, latest announcements,
### attendance rate, unread notifications, outstanding fees
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Student Affairs: the metric catalog (key, titles, unit, drill-down list URL)
GET {{host}}/api/admin/dashboard/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Student Affairs: every metric for a term (default: the active one), optionally one faculty or department
GET {{host}}/api/admin/dashboard/summary?termId={{termId}}&facultyId={{facultyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
